This post is a working reference for adding content. It is marked `draft: true`, so it stays out of the
index, the feed, and the sitemap, and carries a `noindex` tag — but it is still reachable at its URL, so
the layout can be reviewed before anything is published.

## Frontmatter

Every post begins with a frontmatter block. `title`, `description`, and `date` are required; the rest are
optional.

| Field         | Required | Notes                                                      |
| ------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| `title`       | yes      | Heading, page title, feed entry, and card preview.         |
| `description` | yes      | Meta description and the summary shown in the index.       |
| `date`        | yes      | `YYYY-MM-DD`. Drives ordering and the feed's publish date. |
| `updated`     | no       | Adds `dateModified` and the sitemap `lastmod`.             |
| `tags`        | no       | Rendered as chips and emitted as `article:tag`.            |
| `image`       | no       | Overrides the social card, e.g. `/og/my-post.png`.         |
| `draft`       | no       | Hides the post from the index, feed, and sitemap.          |

## Images

Keep images next to the post that uses them. Ordinary markdown syntax is enough — relative paths are
rewritten at build time into responsive markup with AVIF and WebP variants and intrinsic dimensions, so
nothing shifts as the page loads:

![A stylised view of the content pipeline](./pipeline.png)

Add a caption by passing a title, or use `Figure` directly when the image should break out of the prose
column:

<Figure src={pipeline} alt="Source, build, and output stages of the content pipeline" caption="The three stages every post passes through." wide />

Remote and root-relative sources are passed through untouched, so `/static/img/logo.png` still works.

## Footnotes and links

Footnotes use the usual reference syntax and collect at the end of the post with return links.[^images]
Several can point back at the same explanation.[^drafts]

Reference-style links keep prose readable by moving URLs to the [bottom of the file][mdsvex], and ordinary
inline links behave as expected.

## Code

Fenced code blocks are styled to match the rest of the site:

```ts
import { publishedPosts } from '$lib/posts';

const latest = publishedPosts.at(0);
```

> Drafts are the one exception to "what is in the directory is on the site" — they are reachable, but
> never advertised.

[^images]: The rewrite lives in `plugins/vite-svx-images.js`. It runs as a `pre` Vite transform, hoists an
    `?enhanced` import for each relative image, and swaps the markdown for a `Figure`.

[^drafts]: Draft filtering lives in `src/lib/posts.ts`, which the index, the feed, and the sitemap all
    read from.

[mdsvex]: https://mdsvex.pngwn.io
